text:
Looking at the diff: in `parseYamlInteger` (the YAML 1.1 integer parser), the condition guarding sign extraction was changed from `value[0] === "-" || value[0] === "+"` to `value[0] === "-" && value[0] === "+"`. Since a single character can never be both `-` and `+`, this branch is now dead code, so the sign is never stripped.

For base-10 this happens to still work (`parseInt("-42", 10)` is `-42`), but for YAML 1.1's other integer forms the sign must be stripped before radix dispatch: `-0x1F` no longer hits the `0x` branch and instead falls through to `parseInt("-0x1F", 10)` → `-0` instead of `-31`; `-0b101` yields `-0` instead of `-5`; `-010` yields `-10` instead of `-8` (octal); and sexagesimal `-1:30` yields `-30` instead of `-90`. This is observable via `load` with `YAML11_SCHEMA` (the default `CORE_SCHEMA` uses `intCoreTag`, whose parser is untouched, which is why the core test suite stays green).

```json
{"defect": true, "testFile": {"path": "test/core/proof.test.mjs", "content": "import { describe, it } from 'node:test';
import assert from 'node:assert';
import { load, dump, YAML11_SCHEMA } from 'js-yaml';

describe('proof', () => {
  it('fails on the patched build', () => {
    // YAML 1.1 integers with an explicit sign: the sign must be stripped
    // before radix dispatch. With the patched `&&` the branch is dead code,
    // so signed hex/binary/octal/sexagesimal values are parsed wrongly
    // (e.g. -0x1F resolves to -0 instead of -31).
    assert.strictEqual(load('-0x1F', { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA }), -31);
    assert.strictEqual(load('-0b101', { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA }), -5);
    assert.strictEqual(load('-010', { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA }), -8);
    assert.strictEqual(load('-1:30', { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA }), -90);
  });
});
"}, "note": "The `||` to `&&` change makes the sign-stripping branch in parseYamlInteger unreachable, so YAML 1.1 integers with a leading sign are passed to parseInt with the sign still attached; negative hex/binary/octal and sexagesimal forms resolve to wrong values (e.g. load('-0x1F', { schema: YAML11_SCHEMA }) returns -0 instead of -31). The default CORE_SCHEMA parser is unaffected, which is why the existing suite stays green."}
```

